//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Package
// $Module name: cGridSubclassPorter.pkg
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-10-04
//
// Description : ConvertGridSubclassToCodeJock's engine. A workspace's OWN subclass of a legacy grid is
//               ported IN PLACE to the CodeJock grid it maps to - "Class X is a dbGrid" becomes "Class X
//               is a cDbCJGrid", in its own package, keeping its name - and then every object of it is
//               converted with it, all or nothing (design 2026-10-03, built 2026-10-04).
//****************************************************************************
Use cDbGridTocDbCJGrid.pkg
Use cDbListTocDbCJGridPromptList.pkg
Use cGridToCJGrid.pkg
Use Seq_chnl.pkg                  // Seq_New_Channel - the DIR: listing of the run's folders

/* WHY IN PLACE (Nils 2026-10-03: "a subclass can't be blindly swapped for a CodeJock grid class without
   first have converted the cEntryGrid subclass"). An object converter re-based a subclass object on the
   plain CodeJock class and lost what the subclass added - one workspace's dbGrid subclass anchors the
   grid and translates every label and help text through its own language table. So the converters leave
   such objects as they are (cGridToCJGridBase.SubclassToLeave), and this ports the CLASS first:

     Class X is a dbGrid  -> Class X is a cDbCJGrid           Use Dftable.pkg  -> Use cDbCJGrid.pkg
     Class X is a dbList  -> Class X is a cDbCJGridPromptList Use Dfsellst.pkg -> Use cDbCJGridPromptList.pkg
     Class X is a Grid    -> Class X is a cCJGrid             (Windows.pkg stays; Use cCJGrid.pkg added)

   A legacy grid sets its labels and help PER ITEM, a CodeJock grid per COLUMN, so the class's label and
   help hooks move into a new column class in the same package, "XColumn", with only the message names
   changed - their bodies carry over line for line:

     Procedure Set Header_Label Integer iCol String s   -> Procedure Set psCaption String s
     Procedure Set Status_Help Integer iItem String s   -> Procedure Set Status_Help String s
     Function Status_Help Integer iItem Returns String  -> Function Status_Help Returns String
       (its "which item" selection goes - a column IS the item)

   Construct_Object's Set statements go through the object converter's own property mapping; a Set Label
   override is dropped (a CodeJock grid shows no label); ANYTHING ELSE in the class makes it not portable,
   and the run says what. Then the objects: the family's object converter runs with the parameter
   "X,X,XColumn" - the in-place mode: the object keeps "is a X", its Begin_Row columns become XColumn
   objects, and no "behaviour not inherited" TODO is written (cGridToCJGridBase.TransformSource).

   ALL OR NOTHING PER CLASS, because a ported class with unconverted objects does not compile. Before
   anything is written: the class must be portable, no other class may be built on it, no object may sit
   outside the run's files, no object may set a Label, and a dry run of every object must convert it -
   one declined object refuses the whole class. One class's refusal leaves the others alone.

   THE PARAMETER names one class - or is EMPTY, and the run takes every grid subclass its files declare.
   That is how a PLAN run reaches it (2026-10-04): the Check's rows name this function wherever
   SubclassVerdict says the class converts - the class line, and every object of it - and the plan passes
   their files and no class. A refusal whose cause is in the source leaves a marker above the class
   (_WriteMarker), which the next Check reads, so the board says why instead of offering it again.

   A List subclass is not ported yet: a List's objects commonly set Label, which no CodeJock grid shows. */
Class cGridSubclassPorter is a cObject

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        Property String   psClass        ""     // the class being ported, as written in its declaration
        Property String   psSuperLc      ""     // its legacy superclass, lowercase: dbgrid / dblist / grid
        Property String   psTargetGrid   ""
        Property String  psObjectFn     ""    // the object converter of the family, by its function name - for the notes
        Property String   psTargetColumn ""
        Property String   psTargetUse    ""     // the package that defines the target grid class
        Property String   psLegacyUse    ""     // the legacy package swapped out ("" for Grid: Windows.pkg stays)
        Property String   psColumnClass  ""     // "XColumn" when hooks moved, else "" (the standard column)
        Property String   psRefusal      ""     // why the class is not portable ("" = it is)
        Property String[] pasRefusals           // every reason, psRefusal first - the run note counts them
        Property String[] pasPortNotes          // what the port did, for the run notes
        Property Handle   phoConverter   0      // the family's object converter (mapping + in-place objects)
    End_Procedure

    Procedure Destroy
        Send _DropConverter
        Forward Send Destroy
    End_Procedure

    Procedure _DropConverter
        Handle ho
        Get phoConverter to ho
        If (ho <> 0) Begin
            Send Destroy of ho
            Set phoConverter to 0
        End
    End_Procedure

    // *** Small text helpers ***

    // The words of sText, split at spaces and tabs, no empty ones.
    Function _Words String sText Returns String[]
        String[] asRaw asOut
        Integer  i iLast
        Move (StrSplitToArray((Replaces(Character(9), sText, " ")), " ")) to asRaw
        Move (SizeOfArray(asRaw) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (asRaw[i] <> "") ;
                Move asRaw[i] to asOut[-1]
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // The code part of a trimmed line: everything before a "//" comment.
    Function _CodePart String sTrim Returns String
        Integer iPos
        Move (Pos("//", sTrim)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sTrim, (iPos - 1))) to sTrim
        Function_Return (Trim(sTrim))
    End_Function

    // The lowercase tokens of a line's code, split at spaces and the expression punctuation - for "does this
    // line still name X". A dotted Table.Field stays one token.
    Function _CodeTokens String sTrim Returns String[]
        String sT
        Get _CodePart sTrim to sT
        Move (Lowercase(sT)) to sT
        Move (Replaces("(", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces(")", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces(",", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces("+", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces("=", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces("<", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces(">", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces("*", sT, " ")) to sT
        Move (Replaces(";", sT, " ")) to sT
        Function_Return (_Words(Self, sT))
    End_Function

    // Does the line's code name sWordLc (a lowercase token)?
    Function _NamesWord String sTrim String sWordLc Returns Boolean
        String[] asTok
        Get _CodeTokens sTrim to asTok
        Function_Return (SearchArray(sWordLc, asTok) <> -1)
    End_Function

    // The leading whitespace of sLine.
    Function _Indent String sLine Returns String
        Function_Return (Left(sLine, (Length(sLine) - Length(LTrim(sLine)))))
    End_Function

    /* sLine starts with exactly the words asHead (lowercase) and then "to": returns what follows that "to",
       as written, with bOk True. Otherwise "" and bOk False. "Forward Set Header_Label Item Item# to x". */
    Function _RestAfterWords String sLine String[] asHead Boolean ByRef bOk Returns String
        String  sRest sWord
        Integer i iLast iPos

        Move False to bOk
        Move (Trim(Replaces(Character(9), sLine, " "))) to sRest
        Move (SizeOfArray(asHead) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Pos(" ", sRest)) to iPos
            If (iPos = 0) ;
                Function_Return ""
            Move (Left(sRest, (iPos - 1))) to sWord
            If (Lowercase(sWord) <> asHead[i]) ;
                Function_Return ""
            Move (Trim(Mid(sRest, Length(sRest), (iPos + 1)))) to sRest
        Loop
        If (Lowercase(Left(sRest, 3)) <> "to ") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move True to bOk
        Function_Return (Trim(Mid(sRest, Length(sRest), 4)))
    End_Function

    /* A per-item call rewritten to its per-column form. sLine is "<verb> <msg> [Item] <var> to <rest>" (verb
       one or two words, e.g. "forward set", "get"); the result is "<indent><sNew> to <rest>", or "" when the
       line is not that call. Tried with and without the "Item" keyword. */
    Function _RewriteItemCall String sLine String sVerbLc String sMsgLc String sVarLc String sNew Returns String
        String[] asHead asVerb
        String   sRest
        Boolean  bOk
        Integer  i iLast

        Get _Words sVerbLc to asVerb
        Move (SizeOfArray(asVerb) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move asVerb[i] to asHead[-1]
        Loop
        Move sMsgLc to asHead[-1]
        Move "item" to asHead[-1]
        Move sVarLc to asHead[-1]
        Get _RestAfterWords sLine asHead (&bOk) to sRest
        If (bOk = False) Begin
            Move (RemoveFromArray(asHead, (SizeOfArray(asHead) - 2))) to asHead
            Get _RestAfterWords sLine asHead (&bOk) to sRest
        End
        If (bOk = False) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return ((_Indent(Self, sLine)) + sNew + " to " + sRest)
    End_Function

    // The declaration on sTrim, "Class <name> is a(n) <super>": True, with the name and the superclass as
    // written. A commented-out declaration is not one.
    Function _ClassDecl String sTrim String ByRef sName String ByRef sSuper Returns Boolean
        String   sCode
        String[] asW
        Move "" to sName
        Move "" to sSuper
        Get _CodePart sTrim to sCode
        Get _Words sCode to asW
        If (SizeOfArray(asW) < 5) ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Lowercase(asW[0]) <> "class" or Lowercase(asW[2]) <> "is" or (Lowercase(asW[3]) <> "a" and Lowercase(asW[3]) <> "an")) ;
            Function_Return False
        Move asW[1] to sName
        Move asW[4] to sSuper
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    // *** The family ***

    // Sets the targets for a legacy superclass; False when it is not one this ports.
    Function _SetFamily String sSuperLc Returns Boolean
        Handle ho

        Send _DropConverter
        If (sSuperLc = "dbgrid") Begin
            Set psObjectFn     to "RefactorDbGridTocDbCJGrid"
            Set psTargetGrid   to "cDbCJGrid"
            Set psTargetColumn to "cDbCJGridColumn"
            Set psTargetUse    to "cDbCJGrid.pkg"
            Set psLegacyUse    to "Dftable.pkg"
            Get Create (RefClass(cDbGridTocDbCJGrid)) to ho
        End
        Else If (sSuperLc = "dblist") Begin
            Set psObjectFn     to "RefactorDbListTocDbCJGridPromptList"
            Set psTargetGrid   to "cDbCJGridPromptList"
            Set psTargetColumn to "cDbCJGridColumn"
            Set psTargetUse    to "cDbCJGridPromptList.pkg"
            Set psLegacyUse    to "Dfsellst.pkg"
            Get Create (RefClass(cDbListTocDbCJGridPromptList)) to ho
        End
        Else If (sSuperLc = "grid") Begin
            Set psObjectFn     to "RefactorGridToCJGrid"
            Set psTargetGrid   to "cCJGrid"
            Set psTargetColumn to "cCJGridColumn"
            Set psTargetUse    to "cCJGrid.pkg"
            Set psLegacyUse    to ""
            Get Create (RefClass(cGridToCJGrid)) to ho
        End
        Else ;
            Function_Return False
        Set psSuperLc    to sSuperLc
        Set phoConverter to ho
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    Procedure _Refuse String sWhy
        String[] asWhy
        If (psRefusal(Self) = "") ;
            Set psRefusal to sWhy
        Get pasRefusals to asWhy
        If (SearchArray(sWhy, asWhy) = -1) Begin
            Move sWhy to asWhy[-1]
            Set pasRefusals to asWhy
        End
    End_Procedure

    /* psRefusal, and - when the class had more reasons not to port - how many and the first few (2026-11-01): one
       workspace's dbList subclass overrode a dozen dbList internals, and the run note named only its first line, a
       child Array object in Construct_Object, which read like a small thing to fix. */
    Function _RefusalSummary Returns String
        String[] asWhy
        String   sOut
        Integer  i iShown

        Get pasRefusals to asWhy
        Move (psRefusal(Self)) to sOut
        If (SizeOfArray(asWhy) > 1) Begin
            Move (SizeOfArray(asWhy) - 1) to iShown
            If (iShown > 5) ;
                Move 5 to iShown
            Move (sOut + ". " + String(SizeOfArray(asWhy) - 1) + " more reason(s): ") to sOut
            For i from 1 to iShown
                If (i > 1) ;
                    Move (sOut + "; ") to sOut
                Move (sOut + asWhy[i]) to sOut
            Loop
            If ((SizeOfArray(asWhy) - 1) > iShown) ;
                Move (sOut + "; ...") to sOut
        End
        Function_Return sOut
    End_Function

    Procedure _Note String sNote
        String[] asNotes
        Get pasPortNotes to asNotes
        Move sNote to asNotes[-1]
        Set pasPortNotes to asNotes
    End_Procedure

    // *** The class body's members ***

    // Construct_Object / End_Construct_Object: kept, its Set statements through the object converter's own
    // property mapping (translate, comment out with the closest equivalent, or drop - as an object's own Set
    // lines go). Anything but a Forward, a Property, a Set, a comment or a blank line refuses the class.
    Function _PortConstructor String[] asMember Returns String[]
        String[] asOut asTr
        String   sTrim sLow sHint sIndent sLine
        Integer  i iLast j jLast
        Boolean  bOk bRefused
        Handle   hoConv

        Get phoConverter to hoConv
        Move asMember[0] to asOut[-1]
        Move (SizeOfArray(asMember) - 2) to iLast
        For i from 1 to iLast
            Move asMember[i] to sLine
            Move (Trim(sLine))      to sTrim
            Move (Lowercase(sTrim)) to sLow
            If (sLow = "" or Left(sLow, 2) = "//" or Left(sLow, 8) = "forward " or Left(sLow, 9) = "property ") Begin
                Move sLine to asOut[-1]
            End
            Else If (Left(sLow, 4) = "set ") Begin
                Get IsTranslatableGridProperty of hoConv sLow to bOk
                If (bOk = True) Begin
                    Get TranslateGridProperty of hoConv sLine sLow to asTr
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asTr) - 1) to jLast
                    For j from 0 to jLast
                        Move asTr[j] to asOut[-1]
                    Loop
                    Send _Note ("'" + sTrim + "' translated for " + psTargetGrid(Self) + ".")
                End
                Else Begin
                    Get IsCommentOutGridProperty of hoConv sLow to bOk
                    If (bOk = True) Begin
                        Get _Indent sLine to sIndent
                        Move (sIndent + "// " + sTrim) to asOut[-1]
                        Get LegacyOnlyGridPropertyHint of hoConv sLow to sHint
                        If (sHint <> "") ;
                            Move (sIndent + "// TODO: closest " + psTargetGrid(Self) + " equivalent is " + sHint) to asOut[-1]
                        Send _Note ("'" + sTrim + "' commented out - " + psTargetGrid(Self) + " has no such property.")
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Get IsLegacyGridProperty of hoConv sLow to bOk
                        If (bOk = True) ;
                            Send _Note ("'" + sTrim + "' dropped - it means nothing to " + psTargetGrid(Self) + ".")
                        Else ;
                            Move sLine to asOut[-1]
                    End
                End
            End
            // One reason per member: a child object's every line is the same reason.
            Else If (bRefused = False) Begin
                Send _Refuse ("its " + Trim(asMember[0]) + " does more than set properties ('" + sTrim + "')")
                Move True to bRefused
            End
        Loop
        Move asMember[(SizeOfArray(asMember) - 1)] to asOut[-1]
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // The label hook: Set Header_Label <col> <label> -> Set psCaption <label>, its body line for line.
    Function _PortCaptionHook String[] asMember String sTypeLabel String sLabel String sColLc Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        String   sLine sNew
        Integer  i iLast

        Move ((_Indent(Self, asMember[0])) + "Procedure Set psCaption " + sTypeLabel + " " + sLabel) to asOut[-1]
        Move (SizeOfArray(asMember) - 2) to iLast
        For i from 1 to iLast
            Move asMember[i] to sLine
            Get _RewriteItemCall sLine "forward set" "header_label" sColLc "Forward Set psCaption" to sNew
            If (sNew = "") ;
                Get _RewriteItemCall sLine "get" "header_label" sColLc "Get psCaption" to sNew
            If (sNew <> "") ;
                Move sNew to sLine
            Else If (_NamesWord(Self, (Trim(sLine)), sColLc)) ;
                Send _Refuse ("its Set Header_Label uses the column number for more than the label ('" + Trim(sLine) + "')")
            Move sLine to asOut[-1]
        Loop
        Move asMember[(SizeOfArray(asMember) - 1)] to asOut[-1]
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // Set Status_Help <item> <help> -> Set Status_Help <help>.
    Function _PortSetHelpHook String[] asMember String sTypeHelp String sHelp String sItemLc Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        String   sLine sNew
        Integer  i iLast

        Move ((_Indent(Self, asMember[0])) + "Procedure Set Status_Help " + sTypeHelp + " " + sHelp) to asOut[-1]
        Move (SizeOfArray(asMember) - 2) to iLast
        For i from 1 to iLast
            Move asMember[i] to sLine
            Get _RewriteItemCall sLine "forward set" "status_help" sItemLc "Forward Set Status_Help" to sNew
            If (sNew <> "") ;
                Move sNew to sLine
            Else If (_NamesWord(Self, (Trim(sLine)), sItemLc)) ;
                Send _Refuse ("its Set Status_Help uses the item number for more than the help ('" + Trim(sLine) + "')")
            Move sLine to asOut[-1]
        Loop
        Move asMember[(SizeOfArray(asMember) - 1)] to asOut[-1]
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // Is sLow (a lowercase trimmed line) a local declaration - a type, then names?
    Function _IsLocalDecl String sLow Returns Boolean
        String sW
        Get _NthWord of ghoFuncLib sLow 1 to sW
        Function_Return (sW = "integer" or sW = "string" or sW = "number" or sW = "boolean" or sW = "handle" or sW = "date" or sW = "real" or sW = "datetime" or sW = "variant")
    End_Function

    // The index of the End that closes the Begin on asLines[iFrom], -1 when there is none.
    Function _BlockEnd String[] ByRef asLines Integer iFrom Returns Integer
        String[] asW
        Integer  i iLast iDepth
        Move 0 to iDepth
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from iFrom to iLast
            Get _Words (Lowercase(_CodePart(Self, (Trim(asLines[i]))))) to asW
            If (SizeOfArray(asW) > 0) Begin
                If (asW[(SizeOfArray(asW) - 1)] = "begin") ;
                    Increment iDepth
                If (asW[0] = "end") Begin
                    Decrement iDepth
                    If (iDepth = 0) ;
                        Function_Return i
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return -1
    End_Function

    // Every line from iFrom to iTo (exclusive) is removed (abGone) or blank.
    Function _AllGone String[] ByRef asLines Boolean[] ByRef abGone Integer iFrom Integer iTo Returns Boolean
        Integer i
        For i from iFrom to (iTo - 1)
            If (abGone[i] = False and Trim(asLines[i]) <> "") ;
                Function_Return False
        Loop
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    /* Function Status_Help <item> Returns String -> Function Status_Help Returns String. A column IS the item,
       so the body's "which item" selection goes: the locals it fills from the item parameter (Itm, from
       "Move iItem to Itm"), every Move into them, their declarations, and the If / Else Begin..End shells
       those Moves leave empty. "Forward Get Status_Help <item> to x" becomes "Forward Get Status_Help to x".
       Anything still naming the item - or Num_Arguments - refuses the class. */
    Function _PortGetHelpHook String[] asMember String sItemLc String sReturns Returns String[]
        String[]  asBody asOut asW asSel
        Integer[] aiKeep
        Boolean[] abGone
        String    sLine sLow sNew sIndent
        Integer   i iLast j iEnd iNext k
        Boolean   bChanged bBlank bGone bSeek

        // the body alone, between the header and the end
        Move (SizeOfArray(asMember) - 2) to iLast
        For i from 1 to iLast
            Move asMember[i] to asBody[-1]
        Loop
        Move (SizeOfArray(asBody) - 1) to iLast
        // the selector locals
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Get _Words (Lowercase(_CodePart(Self, (Trim(asBody[i]))))) to asW
            If (SizeOfArray(asW) = 4) Begin
                If (asW[0] = "move" and asW[1] = sItemLc and asW[2] = "to" and SearchArray(asW[3], asSel) = -1) ;
                    Move asW[3] to asSel[-1]
            End
        Loop
        // mark: every Move into a selector, and a selector's declaration (the name taken out of a list)
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move False to abGone[i]
        Loop
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(_CodePart(Self, (Trim(asBody[i]))))) to sLow
            Get _Words sLow to asW
            If (SizeOfArray(asW) = 4) Begin
                If (asW[0] = "move" and asW[2] = "to" and SearchArray(asW[3], asSel) <> -1) ;
                    Move True to abGone[i]
            End
            If (abGone[i] = False and SizeOfArray(asW) > 1 and _IsLocalDecl(Self, sLow)) Begin
                Move (ResizeArray(aiKeep, 0)) to aiKeep
                For j from 1 to (SizeOfArray(asW) - 1)
                    If (SearchArray(asW[j], asSel) = -1) ;
                        Move j to aiKeep[-1]
                Loop
                If (SizeOfArray(aiKeep) = 0) Begin
                    Move True to abGone[i]
                End
                Else If (SizeOfArray(aiKeep) < (SizeOfArray(asW) - 1)) Begin
                    // keep the other names, in their own casing
                    Get _Words (Trim(asBody[i])) to asW
                    Get _Indent asBody[i] to sIndent
                    Move (sIndent + asW[0]) to sNew
                    For j from 0 to (SizeOfArray(aiKeep) - 1)
                        Move (sNew + " " + asW[aiKeep[j]]) to sNew
                    Loop
                    Move sNew to asBody[i]
                End
            End
        Loop
        // the If / Else shells the removed Moves leave empty
        Repeat
            Move False to bChanged
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (abGone[i] = False) Begin
                    Get _Words (Lowercase(_CodePart(Self, (Trim(asBody[i]))))) to asW
                    If (SizeOfArray(asW) > 1) Begin
                        If (asW[0] = "if" and asW[(SizeOfArray(asW) - 1)] = "begin") Begin
                            Get _BlockEnd (&asBody) i to iEnd
                            Move False to bGone
                            If (iEnd > i) ;
                                Get _AllGone (&asBody) (&abGone) (i + 1) iEnd to bGone
                            If (bGone = True) Begin
                                // ...and its Else Begin..End, when that is empty too
                                Move (iEnd + 1) to iNext
                                Move True to bSeek
                                While (bSeek = True)
                                    If (iNext > iLast) ;
                                        Move False to bSeek
                                    Else If (Trim(asBody[iNext]) <> "") ;
                                        Move False to bSeek
                                    Else ;
                                        Increment iNext
                                Loop
                                If (iNext <= iLast) Begin
                                    Get _Words (Lowercase(_CodePart(Self, (Trim(asBody[iNext]))))) to asW
                                    If (SizeOfArray(asW) = 2 and asW[0] = "else" and asW[1] = "begin") Begin
                                        Get _BlockEnd (&asBody) iNext to k
                                        Move False to bGone
                                        If (k > iNext) ;
                                            Get _AllGone (&asBody) (&abGone) (iNext + 1) k to bGone
                                        If (bGone = True) Begin
                                            For j from iNext to k
                                                Move True to abGone[j]
                                            Loop
                                        End
                                        Else ;
                                            Move -1 to iEnd      // a live Else: the If shell must stay
                                    End
                                End
                                If (iEnd > i) Begin
                                    For j from i to iEnd
                                        Move True to abGone[j]
                                    Loop
                                    Move True to bChanged
                                End
                            End
                        End
                    End
                End
            Loop
        Until (bChanged = False)
        // the header, the kept lines (the Forward Get rewritten), the end; one blank line where several meet
        Move ((_Indent(Self, asMember[0])) + "Function Status_Help Returns " + sReturns) to asOut[-1]
        Move False to bBlank
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (abGone[i] = False) Begin
                Move asBody[i] to sLine
                If (Trim(sLine) = "") Begin
                    If (bBlank = False) ;
                        Move sLine to asOut[-1]
                    Move True to bBlank
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move False to bBlank
                    Get _RewriteItemCall sLine "forward get" "status_help" sItemLc "Forward Get Status_Help" to sNew
                    For j from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asSel) - 1)
                        If (sNew = "") ;
                            Get _RewriteItemCall sLine "forward get" "status_help" asSel[j] "Forward Get Status_Help" to sNew
                    Loop
                    If (sNew <> "") ;
                        Move sNew to sLine
                    Else Begin
                        If (_NamesWord(Self, (Trim(sLine)), sItemLc) or _NamesWord(Self, (Trim(sLine)), "num_arguments")) ;
                            Send _Refuse ("its Function Status_Help uses the item number for more than the help ('" + Trim(sLine) + "')")
                        For j from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asSel) - 1)
                            If (_NamesWord(Self, (Trim(sLine)), asSel[j])) ;
                                Send _Refuse ("its Function Status_Help uses the item number for more than the help ('" + Trim(sLine) + "')")
                        Loop
                    End
                    Move sLine to asOut[-1]
                End
            End
        Loop
        Move asMember[(SizeOfArray(asMember) - 1)] to asOut[-1]
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    /* One member of the class body, sorted: kept in the grid class (Construct_Object), moved into the column
       class (a hook - returned in asHook), dropped (Set Label) or refused. Returns the lines the grid class
       keeps; asHook comes back with the column class's version, or empty. */
    Function _PortMember String[] asMember String[] ByRef asHook Returns String[]
        String[] asW asNone
        String   sHead sMethod
        Integer  iW
        Boolean  bSet

        Move asNone to asHook
        Get _Words (_CodePart(Self, (Trim(asMember[0])))) to asW
        Move (SizeOfArray(asW)) to iW
        Move (Trim(asMember[0])) to sHead
        If (iW < 2) Begin
            Send _Refuse ("'" + sHead + "' - a member this converter does not read")
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        Move (Lowercase(asW[0]) = "procedure" and Lowercase(asW[1]) = "set") to bSet
        If (bSet = True and iW >= 3) ;
            Move (Lowercase(asW[2])) to sMethod
        Else ;
            Move (Lowercase(asW[1])) to sMethod
        // Construct_Object / End_Construct_Object: kept, the Sets mapped
        If (bSet = False and Lowercase(asW[0]) = "procedure" and (sMethod = "construct_object" or sMethod = "end_construct_object") and iW = 2) ;
            Function_Return (_PortConstructor(Self, asMember))
        // Procedure Set Header_Label <type> <col> <type> <label>
        If (bSet = True and sMethod = "header_label" and iW = 7) Begin
            Get _PortCaptionHook asMember asW[5] asW[6] (Lowercase(asW[4])) to asHook
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        // Procedure Set Status_Help <type> <item> <type> <help>
        If (bSet = True and sMethod = "status_help" and iW = 7) Begin
            Get _PortSetHelpHook asMember asW[5] asW[6] (Lowercase(asW[4])) to asHook
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        // Function Status_Help <type> <item> Returns <type>
        If (bSet = False and Lowercase(asW[0]) = "function" and sMethod = "status_help" and iW = 6) Begin
            If (Lowercase(asW[4]) = "returns") Begin
                Get _PortGetHelpHook asMember (Lowercase(asW[3])) asW[5] to asHook
                Function_Return asNone
            End
        End
        // Procedure Set Label <type> <label>: a CodeJock grid shows no label
        If (bSet = True and sMethod = "label" and iW = 5) Begin
            Send _Note ("its Set Label override is dropped - a " + psTargetGrid(Self) + " shows no label.")
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        Send _Refuse ("'" + sHead + "' - no " + psTargetGrid(Self) + " counterpart this converter knows")
        Function_Return asNone
    End_Function

    // *** The class ***

    /* _PortClassLines with the text masked (2026-10-30, cRefactorFuncLib's MaskForTransform): a block comment's, a
       report image's and a string's text and the macro code are masked away while the class is ported and put back
       after - a commented-out procedure is no code to port, and its text is never refactored. */
    Function PortClassSource String[] asLines String sClass Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        tWholeFileMask Mask
        Integer iMacro iLost

        Get MaskForTransform of ghoFuncLib (&asLines) (&Mask) to iMacro
        Get _PortClassLines asLines sClass to asOut
        If (SizeOfArray(asOut) > 0) Begin
            Get UnmaskAfterTransform of ghoFuncLib (&asOut) (&Mask) to iLost
            If (iLost > 0) ;
                Send _Note (String(iLost) * "line(s) of comment, image or string text or macro code the conversion had removed were put back where they were - check the file.")
        End
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    /* The file asLines with class sClass ported in place, or an EMPTY array with psRefusal saying why. Fills
       psColumnClass ("" when no hook moved) and pasPortNotes. The file's other classes and code are untouched. */
    Function _PortClassLines String[] asLines String sClass Returns String[]
        String[] asOut asNone asKeep asHook asHooks asMember asNotes
        String   sName sSuper sTrim sLow sIndent sMemberIndent sLine sUsed sLegacy sTargetUse sColumn sNote
        Integer  i iLast iClass iEnd k kLast iUse iLastUse iFirstHook iUseDepth
        Boolean  bUseInBlock
        Boolean  bFound bStill bTargetUsed bGone
        Handle   hoConv

        Set psRefusal to ""
        Set pasRefusals to asNone
        Set psColumnClass to ""
        Set pasPortNotes to asNotes
        Move -1 to iClass
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (iClass = -1) Begin
                Get _ClassDecl (Trim(asLines[i])) (&sName) (&sSuper) to bFound
                If (bFound = True and Lowercase(sName) = Lowercase(sClass)) Begin
                    Move i to iClass
                    Set psClass to sName
                End
            End
        Loop
        If (iClass = -1) Begin
            Send _Refuse ("Class " + sClass + " is not declared in this file")
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        Get _ClassDecl (Trim(asLines[iClass])) (&sName) (&sSuper) to bFound
        If (_SetFamily(Self, (Lowercase(sSuper))) = False) Begin
            If (Lowercase(sSuper) = "list") ;
                Send _Refuse (sName + " is a List subclass - those are not converted yet: their objects commonly set a Label, which no CodeJock grid shows")
            Else ;
                Send _Refuse (sName + " is a " + sSuper + ", not a dbGrid, dbList or Grid")
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        Get phoConverter to hoConv
        Move -1 to iEnd
        For i from (iClass + 1) to iLast
            If (iEnd = -1 and Left(Lowercase(Trim(asLines[i])), 9) = "end_class") ;
                Move i to iEnd
        Loop
        If (iEnd = -1) Begin
            Send _Refuse ("Class " + sName + " has no End_Class")
            Function_Return asNone
        End

        // The body: comments and blank lines kept, members sorted (_PortMember), anything else refused.
        Move "" to sMemberIndent
        Move -1 to iFirstHook
        Move (iClass + 1) to i
        While (i < iEnd)
            Move asLines[i] to sLine
            Move (Trim(sLine))      to sTrim
            Move (Lowercase(sTrim)) to sLow
            If (sLow = "" or Left(sLow, 2) = "//") Begin
                Move sLine to asKeep[-1]
                Increment i
            End
            Else If (Left(sLow, 2) = "/*") Begin
                Repeat
                    Move asLines[i] to asKeep[-1]
                    Increment i
                Until (i >= iEnd or (Lowercase(asLines[(i - 1)]) contains "*/"))
            End
            Else If (Left(sLow, 10) = "procedure " or Left(sLow, 9) = "function ") Begin
                If (sMemberIndent = "") ;
                    Get _Indent sLine to sMemberIndent
                Move (ResizeArray(asMember, 0)) to asMember
                Repeat
                    Move asLines[i] to asMember[-1]
                    Move (Lowercase(Trim(asLines[i]))) to sLow
                    Increment i
                Until (i >= iEnd or Left(sLow, 13) = "end_procedure" or Left(sLow, 12) = "end_function")
                Get _PortMember asMember (&asHook) to asMember
                Move (SizeOfArray(asMember) = 0) to bGone
                Move (SizeOfArray(asMember) - 1) to kLast
                For k from 0 to kLast
                    Move asMember[k] to asKeep[-1]
                Loop
                If (SizeOfArray(asHook) > 0) Begin
                    If (iFirstHook = -1) Begin
                        Move (SizeOfArray(asKeep)) to iFirstHook
                        Move "" to asKeep[-1]       // the place the note goes, filled in below
                        Move False to bGone         // the note takes the member's place, its blank lines too
                    End
                    If (SizeOfArray(asHooks) > 0) ;
                        Move "" to asHooks[-1]
                    For k from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asHook) - 1)
                        Move asHook[k] to asHooks[-1]
                    Loop
                End
                /* A member that LEFT the class - moved to the column class, or dropped - takes the blank
                   lines after it along: they only separated it from the next member, and kept, they piled
                   up above End_Class (the first live run, 2026-10-04: four of them). */
                If (bGone = True) Begin
                    While (i < iEnd and Trim(asLines[i]) = "")
                        Increment i
                    Loop
                End
            End
            Else Begin
                Send _Refuse ("'" + sTrim + "' in its class body - not something this converter carries")
                Increment i
            End
        Loop
        If (psRefusal(Self) <> "") ;
            Function_Return asNone

        If (SizeOfArray(asHooks) > 0) Begin
            Move (sName + "Column") to sColumn
            Set psColumnClass to sColumn
            Move (sMemberIndent + "// The label and help hooks are in " + sColumn + ", below: a CodeJock grid sets them per column.") to asKeep[iFirstHook]
        End
        Get psLegacyUse to sLegacy
        Get psTargetUse to sTargetUse

        // Assemble: the lines before the class, the class (its superclass swapped), the column class, the rest.
        For i from 0 to (iClass - 1)
            Move asLines[i] to asOut[-1]
        Loop
        Get _Indent asLines[iClass] to sIndent
        Move (sIndent + "Class " + sName + " is a " + psTargetGrid(Self)) to sLine
        Get _CodePart (Trim(asLines[iClass])) to sTrim
        If (Length(sTrim) < Length(Trim(asLines[iClass]))) ;
            Move (sLine + "  " + Trim(Right((Trim(asLines[iClass])), (Length(Trim(asLines[iClass])) - Length(sTrim))))) to sLine
        Move sLine to asOut[-1]
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asKeep) - 1)
            Move asKeep[i] to asOut[-1]
        Loop
        Move asLines[iEnd] to asOut[-1]
        If (SizeOfArray(asHooks) > 0) Begin
            Move "" to asOut[-1]
            Move (sIndent + "Class " + sColumn + " is a " + psTargetColumn(Self)) to asOut[-1]
            For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asHooks) - 1)
                Move asHooks[i] to asOut[-1]
            Loop
            Move (sIndent + "End_Class") to asOut[-1]
        End
        For i from (iEnd + 1) to iLast
            Move asLines[i] to asOut[-1]
        Loop

        /* THE USE LINE. The legacy package the family names (Dftable.pkg / Dfsellst.pkg) is swapped in place
           for the target's when nothing else in the file still needs it - the object converter's own test
           (LegacyPackageStillUsed); otherwise it stays and the target joins it. Without a legacy Use - Grid,
           whose class lives in Windows.pkg, or a class that relied on another file's Use - the target is
           added after the last Use above the class, or right above the class when there is none. */
        Move -1 to iUse
        Move -1 to iLastUse
        Move False to bTargetUsed
        For i from 0 to (iClass - 1)
            Send rfUseAnchorStep asOut[i] i (&iUseDepth) (&bUseInBlock) (&iLastUse)
            Get UsePackageOnLine of hoConv asOut[i] to sUsed
            If (sUsed <> "") Begin
                If (Lowercase(sUsed) = Lowercase(sTargetUse)) ;
                    Move True to bTargetUsed
                If (sLegacy <> "" and (Lowercase(sUsed) = Lowercase(sLegacy) or Lowercase(sUsed + ".pkg") = Lowercase(sLegacy))) ;
                    Move i to iUse
            End
        Loop
        If (bTargetUsed = False) Begin
            Move False to bStill
            If (iUse <> -1) ;
                Get LegacyPackageStillUsed of hoConv (&asOut) sLegacy to bStill
            If (iUse <> -1 and bStill = False) Begin
                Move ((_Indent(Self, asOut[iUse])) + "Use " + sTargetUse) to asOut[iUse]
                Send _Note ("Use " + sLegacy + " -> Use " + sTargetUse + ".")
            End
            Else Begin
                If (iUse <> -1) ;
                    Move iUse to iLastUse
                If (iLastUse <> -1) ;
                    Move (InsertInArray(asOut, (iLastUse + 1), ((_Indent(Self, asOut[iLastUse])) + "Use " + sTargetUse))) to asOut
                Else ;
                    Move (InsertInArray(asOut, iClass, (sIndent + "Use " + sTargetUse))) to asOut
                Send _Note ("Use " + sTargetUse + " added.")
            End
        End
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // *** The run ***

    // Is the trimmed line an object of sClassLc, as the in-place object converter will see it?
    Function _IsObjectOfClass String sTrim String sClassLc Returns Boolean
        String[] asW
        Get _Words (_CodePart(Self, sTrim)) to asW
        If (SizeOfArray(asW) < 5) ;
            Function_Return False
        Function_Return (Lowercase(asW[0]) = "object" and Lowercase(asW[2]) = "is" and (Lowercase(asW[3]) = "a" or Lowercase(asW[3]) = "an") and Lowercase(asW[4]) = sClassLc)
    End_Function

    /* The objects of sClassLc in asLines: their count, and (asLabelSites, "line N") each one that sets its own
       Label - in its own body, not in a nested object's. */
    Function _ScanObjects String[] ByRef asLines String sClassLc String[] ByRef asLabelSites Returns Integer
        Integer i iLast iDepth iCount
        String  sLow
        Move 0 to iCount
        Move 0 to iDepth
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(Trim(asLines[i]))) to sLow
            If (iDepth > 0) Begin
                If (Left(sLow, 7) = "object ") ;
                    Increment iDepth
                Else If (Left(sLow, 10) = "end_object") ;
                    Decrement iDepth
                Else If (iDepth = 1 and Left(sLow, 10) = "set label ") ;
                    Move ("line " + String(i + 1)) to asLabelSites[-1]
            End
            Else If (_IsObjectOfClass(Self, (Trim(asLines[i])), sClassLc)) Begin
                Increment iCount
                Move 1 to iDepth
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return iCount
    End_Function

    /* _ScanObjects for SEVERAL classes in one walk over the lines (the run reads each file once, whatever the
       number of classes): aiCount[k] objects of asCandLc[k] (lowercase names), and asSites[k] the "line N" of
       each one that sets its own Label. Both come back sized to asCandLc. */
    Procedure _ScanObjectsAll String[] ByRef asLines String[] ByRef asCandLc Integer[] ByRef aiCount String[][] ByRef asSites
        String[] asW
        String   sLow
        Integer  i iLast iDepth iAt iCand

        Move (SizeOfArray(asCandLc)) to iCand
        Move (ResizeArray(aiCount, 0))     to aiCount
        Move (ResizeArray(aiCount, iCand)) to aiCount
        Move (ResizeArray(asSites, 0))     to asSites
        Move (ResizeArray(asSites, iCand)) to asSites
        Move 0  to iDepth
        Move -1 to iAt
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(Trim(Replaces(Character(9), asLines[i], " ")))) to sLow
            If (iDepth > 0) Begin
                If (Left(sLow, 7) = "object ") ;
                    Increment iDepth
                Else If (Left(sLow, 10) = "end_object") ;
                    Decrement iDepth
                Else If (iDepth = 1 and Left(sLow, 10) = "set label ") ;
                    Move ("line " + String(i + 1)) to asSites[iAt][SizeOfArray(asSites[iAt])]
            End
            Else If (Left(sLow, 7) = "object ") Begin
                Get _Words (_CodePart(Self, sLow)) to asW
                If (SizeOfArray(asW) >= 5) Begin
                    If (asW[2] = "is" and (asW[3] = "a" or asW[3] = "an")) Begin
                        Move (SearchArray(asW[4], asCandLc)) to iAt
                        If (iAt <> -1) Begin
                            Move (aiCount[iAt] + 1) to aiCount[iAt]
                            Move 1 to iDepth
                        End
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // The bare file names in sFolder (DIR: lists them one to a line; a missing folder lists nothing).
    Function _FolderFileNames String sFolder Returns String[]
        Integer  iCh
        String   sLine
        String[] asFiles
        Move (Seq_New_Channel()) to iCh
        If (iCh < 0) ;
            Function_Return asFiles
        Direct_Input channel iCh ("DIR:" + sFolder + "*.*")
        If (not(SeqEof)) Begin
            Readln channel iCh sLine
            While (not(SeqEof))
                If (Trim(sLine) <> "") ;
                    Move (Trim(sLine)) to asFiles[-1]
                Readln channel iCh sLine
            Loop
        End
        Close_Input channel iCh
        Send Seq_Release_Channel iCh
        Function_Return asFiles
    End_Function

    /* Every "Class X is a Y" of asLines, appended to three parallel lists: the name and the superclass as
       written, the file beside them. */
    Procedure _CollectClassDecls String[] ByRef asLines String sFile String[] ByRef asNames String[] ByRef asSupers String[] ByRef asDeclFiles
        String  sName sSuper
        Integer i iLast
        Boolean bFound

        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Pos("class", Lowercase(asLines[i])) > 0) Begin
                Get _ClassDecl (Trim(Replaces(Character(9), asLines[i], " "))) (&sName) (&sSuper) to bFound
                If (bFound = True) Begin
                    Move sName  to asNames[-1]
                    Move sSuper to asSupers[-1]
                    Move sFile  to asDeclFiles[-1]
                End
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // The 0-based line that declares sClass in asLines; -1 when none does.
    Function _ClassLine String[] ByRef asLines String sClass Returns Integer
        String  sName sSuper sClassLc
        Integer i iLast
        Boolean bFound

        Move (Lowercase(sClass)) to sClassLc
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Pos("class", Lowercase(asLines[i])) > 0) Begin
                Get _ClassDecl (Trim(Replaces(Character(9), asLines[i], " "))) (&sName) (&sSuper) to bFound
                If (bFound = True) Begin
                    If (Lowercase(sName) = sClassLc) ;
                        Function_Return i
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return -1
    End_Function

    /* THE NOTE A REFUSED RUN LEAVES ABOVE THE CLASS. A refusal whose cause is in the source - an object that
       sets its own Label, an object the converter declines - would otherwise come back on every Check as the
       same offer and be refused again by every run. The marker is the standing one, '// TODO (DFRefactor):
       NOT converted - <reason>' (cGridToCJGridBase.AppendDeclineMarker): the scan and the analyzer already
       read it above a declaration, and SubclassVerdict reads it here, so the class's rows say why instead of
       offering the run. Deleting the line is how the user asks again. */
    Function _MarkerLead Returns String
        Function_Return ("/" + "/ TODO (DFRefactor): NOT converted - ")
    End_Function

    // The reason on the marker line directly above sClass's declaration; "" when there is no marker.
    Function _MarkerReason String[] ByRef asLines String sClass Returns String
        String  sAbove sLead
        Integer iClass

        Get _ClassLine (&asLines) sClass to iClass
        If (iClass < 1) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Trim(Replaces(Character(9), asLines[iClass - 1], " "))) to sAbove
        Get _MarkerLead to sLead
        If (Lowercase(Left(sAbove, Length(sLead))) <> Lowercase(sLead)) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (Trim(Right(sAbove, (Length(sAbove) - Length(sLead)))))
    End_Function

    // Writes the marker above sClass's declaration in sClassFile (replacing an earlier one). Never in a
    // read-only run.
    Procedure _WriteMarker String sClassFile String sClass String sReason
        String[] asLines
        String   sLine sOld
        Integer  iClass
        Boolean  bOk bUtf8

        If (pbReadOnly(ghoFuncLib) = True) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sClassFile)) to asLines
        Get _ClassLine (&asLines) sClass to iClass
        If (iClass = -1) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move ((_Indent(Self, asLines[iClass])) + (_MarkerLead(Self)) + sReason) to sLine
        Get _MarkerReason (&asLines) sClass to sOld
        If (sOld <> "") ;
            Move sLine to asLines[iClass - 1]
        Else ;
            Move (InsertInArray(asLines, iClass, sLine)) to asLines
        Move (rfFileHasBOM(sClassFile)) to bUtf8
        Get _GuardedWriteEncodedFile of ghoFuncLib sClassFile (&asLines) bUtf8 to bOk
    End_Procedure

    /* CAN sClass BE CONVERTED IN PLACE? "" when it can; otherwise why not, worded to follow "... cannot be
       converted in place: ". asLines is its file. Asked by the run before it touches anything, and by the
       Check (cDeepScanner, through the function library), so a row offers the conversion only where the run
       will make it. Four questions, none of which reads another file:
         - does the class body port (PortClassSource)?
         - did an earlier run leave its note above the class (_MarkerReason)?
         - is another class built on it? Its objects would keep their old bodies under a converted base,
           so a class with subclasses of its own is not converted yet;
         - is the name of the column class the port would create already taken?
       The last two are asked of the declarations the caller collected - asNames / asSupers / asDeclFiles,
       parallel, any letter case. Leaves the family set for sClass. */
    Function SubclassVerdict String[] ByRef asLines String sClass String[] ByRef asNames String[] ByRef asSupers String[] ByRef asDeclFiles Returns String
        String[] asPorted
        String   sClassLc sMarker
        Integer  i iLast

        Get PortClassSource asLines sClass to asPorted
        If (SizeOfArray(asPorted) = 0) ;
            Function_Return (psRefusal(Self))
        Get _MarkerReason (&asLines) sClass to sMarker
        If (sMarker <> "") ;
            Function_Return ("an earlier run left it as it is, and the note it wrote above the class says why - " + sMarker)
        Move (Lowercase(sClass)) to sClassLc
        Move (SizeOfArray(asNames) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Lowercase(asSupers[i]) = sClassLc) ;
                Function_Return (asNames[i] + " (" + asDeclFiles[i] + ") is built on it, and a class with subclasses of its own is not converted yet")
        Loop
        If (psColumnClass(Self) <> "") Begin
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (Lowercase(asNames[i]) = (sClassLc + "column")) ;
                    Function_Return ("the class " + asNames[i] + " already exists (" + asDeclFiles[i] + "), and the port would create a column class of that name")
            Loop
        End
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    /* The files of the run's folders that are NOT in the run, read once (only the extensions the run itself
       carries): their class declarations join asNames / asSupers / asDeclFiles, and for each class in
       asCandLc the files that hold an object of it join asOutside[k] - the reason a run must refuse that
       class: those objects would keep their old bodies under a converted class. Nothing is read without a
       run context (pasRunFolders). asOutside comes in sized to asCandLc. */
    Procedure _ScanOutsideRun String[] asRunLc String[] ByRef asCandLc String[] ByRef asNames String[] ByRef asSupers String[] ByRef asDeclFiles String[][] ByRef asOutside
        String[]   asFolders asFileNames asExts asLines
        String[][] asNoSites
        Integer[]  aiCount
        String     sFolder sPath sExt
        Integer    i j k iPos iCand
        Boolean    bCancel

        Move (SizeOfArray(asCandLc)) to iCand
        Get pasRunFolders of ghoFuncLib to asFolders
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asRunLc) - 1)
            Move (RightPos(".", asRunLc[i])) to iPos
            If (iPos > 0) Begin
                Move (Mid(asRunLc[i], Length(asRunLc[i]), iPos)) to sExt
                If (SearchArray(sExt, asExts) = -1) ;
                    Move sExt to asExts[-1]
            End
        Loop
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asFolders) - 1)
            Move asFolders[i] to sFolder
            If (Right(sFolder, 1) <> "\") ;
                Move (sFolder + "\") to sFolder
            Get _FolderFileNames sFolder to asFileNames
            For j from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asFileNames) - 1)
                Move (sFolder + asFileNames[j]) to sPath
                Move (RightPos(".", asFileNames[j])) to iPos
                Move "" to sExt
                If (iPos > 0) ;
                    Move (Lowercase(Mid(asFileNames[j], Length(asFileNames[j]), iPos))) to sExt
                If (sExt <> "" and SearchArray(sExt, asExts) <> -1 and SearchArray((Lowercase(sPath)), asRunLc) = -1) Begin
                    If (Mod(j, 20) = 0) ;
                        Send _Panel "Looking at the files outside the run:" sPath (j + 1) (SizeOfArray(asFileNames))
                    Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sPath)) to asLines
                    Send _CollectClassDecls (&asLines) sPath (&asNames) (&asSupers) (&asDeclFiles)
                    Send _ScanObjectsAll (&asLines) (&asCandLc) (&aiCount) (&asNoSites)
                    For k from 0 to (iCand - 1)
                        If (aiCount[k] > 0) ;
                            Move sPath to asOutside[k][SizeOfArray(asOutside[k])]
                    Loop
                End
                If (ghoEngine <> 0) Begin
                    Get pbUserCancelRequested of ghoEngine to bCancel
                    If (bCancel = True) ;
                        Procedure_Return
                End
            Loop
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // A run note under the running function's name - outside a run there is nothing to note into.
    Procedure _RunNote String sNote
        String sFn
        If (ghoFuncLib = 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Get psExecutionContext of ghoFuncLib to sFn
        If (Trim(sFn) <> "") ;
            Send AddRunNote of ghoFuncLib sFn sNote
    End_Procedure

    Procedure _Panel String sTitle String sFile Integer iAt Integer iOf
        If (ghoStatusPanel = 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Set Caption_Text   of ghoStatusPanel to ("Grid subclass - File No:" * String(iAt) * "of:" * String(iOf))
        Set Title_Text     of ghoStatusPanel to sTitle
        Set TableName_Text of ghoStatusPanel to sFile
    End_Procedure

    // True when the user asked the engine to cancel (never Cancel_Check - that one is the engine's own).
    Function _CancelAsked Returns Boolean
        Boolean bCancel
        Move False to bCancel
        If (ghoEngine <> 0) ;
            Get pbUserCancelRequested of ghoEngine to bCancel
        Function_Return bCancel
    End_Function

    /* ONE CLASS, once the run's passes have found its objects: the last checks, then the write. Returns the
       number of objects converted. 0 on a refusal, which converts nothing: the run notes say why, and for a
       cause that sits in the source a marker above the class says it to the next Check as well.
         asObjFiles    the run's files that hold objects of it
         asLabelSites  "<file> line N" of each object that sets its own Label
         asOutside     files outside the run that hold objects of it */
    Function _ConvertOneClass String sClass String sClassFile String[] asObjFiles String[] asLabelSites String[] asOutside Returns Integer
        String[] asLines asPorted asNotes
        String   sColumn sParam sDeclined sWhy
        Integer  i iObjects iFileObjects iDeclined iConverted
        Boolean  bOk bUtf8
        Handle   hoConv

        // Read HERE, not earlier: an earlier class of this run may have been written into the same file.
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sClassFile)) to asLines
        Get PortClassSource asLines sClass to asPorted
        If (SizeOfArray(asPorted) = 0) Begin
            Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - " + sClass + " (" + sClassFile + "): " + _RefusalSummary(Self) + ".")
            Function_Return 0
        End
        Get psColumnClass to sColumn
        If (sColumn = "") ;
            Get psTargetColumn to sColumn
        Get phoConverter to hoConv

        // Objects that set their own Label: a CodeJock grid shows none.
        If (SizeOfArray(asLabelSites) > 0) Begin
            Move (String(SizeOfArray(asLabelSites)) + " object(s) of " + sClass + " set their own Label, which a " + psTargetGrid(Self) + " does not show - the first at " + asLabelSites[0] + ". Settle those, then remove this line and run Check again.") to sWhy
            Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - " + sClass + ": " + sWhy + " The class converts with all of its objects or not at all.")
            Send _WriteMarker sClassFile sClass sWhy
            Function_Return 0
        End
        // Objects outside the run: the run's own selection, so nothing is written into the source for it.
        If (SizeOfArray(asOutside) > 0) Begin
            Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - " + sClass + ": " + String(SizeOfArray(asOutside)) + " file(s) with objects of it are outside this run, the first " + asOutside[0] + ". They would keep their old bodies under the converted class - include every file that holds its objects, and run again.")
            Function_Return 0
        End

        // The dry run: every object must convert - one declined object refuses the whole class.
        Move (sClass + "," + sClass + "," + sColumn) to sParam
        Get ParseAndSetParameter of hoConv sParam to bOk
        If (bOk = False) ;
            Function_Return 0
        Move 0 to iObjects
        Move 0 to iDeclined
        Move "" to sDeclined
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asObjFiles) - 1)
            Send _Panel ("Trying the conversion of " + sClass + " objects in:") asObjFiles[i] (i + 1) (SizeOfArray(asObjFiles))
            Send ReadFile of hoConv asObjFiles[i]
            Get TransformSource of hoConv to iFileObjects
            Add iFileObjects to iObjects
            If (piDeclineMarkers(hoConv) > 0) Begin
                Add (piDeclineMarkers(hoConv)) to iDeclined
                If (sDeclined = "") ;
                    Move asObjFiles[i] to sDeclined
            End
            If (_CancelAsked(Self) = True) ;
                Function_Return 0
        Loop
        If (iDeclined > 0) Begin
            Move (String(iDeclined) + " object(s) of " + sClass + " cannot be converted, the first in " + sDeclined + ". Settle those (the run notes of the run that wrote this say why), then remove this line and run Check again.") to sWhy
            Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - " + sClass + ": " + String(iDeclined) + " object(s) of it cannot be converted (the notes above say why), the first in " + sDeclined + ". The class converts with all of its objects or not at all.")
            Send _WriteMarker sClassFile sClass sWhy
            Function_Return 0
        End

        // The write: the class, then every object. A read-only run stops here - its dry run was the answer.
        If (pbReadOnly(ghoFuncLib) = False) Begin
            Move (rfFileHasBOM(sClassFile)) to bUtf8
            Get _GuardedWriteEncodedFile of ghoFuncLib sClassFile (&asPorted) bUtf8 to bOk
            If (bOk = False) Begin
                Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - " + sClassFile + " could not be written. " + sClass + " was left as it is.")
                Function_Return 0
            End
            Move 0 to iConverted
            If (SizeOfArray(asObjFiles) > 0) ;
                Get TransformFiles of hoConv asObjFiles sParam to iConverted
        End
        Else ;
            Move iObjects to iConverted
        Send _RunNote (sClass + " is a " + psTargetGrid(Self) + " now, in " + sClassFile + If((psColumnClass(Self) <> ""), (", its label and help hooks in the new " + psColumnClass(Self)), "") + ". " + String(iConverted) + " object(s) of it converted by " + psObjectFn(Self) + ", in " + String(SizeOfArray(asObjFiles)) + " file(s).")
        Get pasPortNotes to asNotes
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asNotes) - 1)
            Send _RunNote (sClass + ": " + asNotes[i])
        Loop
        Function_Return iConverted
    End_Function

    /* THE RUN: ConvertGridSubclassToCodeJock. sParameter names ONE class - or is EMPTY, and the run takes every
       grid subclass its files declare (how a plan run reaches it: the plan passes the files its rows name
       and no class). Each class converts with all of its objects or not at all, and one class's refusal
       leaves the others alone. Returns the number of objects converted.

       The files are read a fixed number of times, whatever the number of classes: once for the class
       declarations, once for the objects of every class together, and the files outside the run once. */
    Function ConvertSubclass String[] asFiles String sParameter Returns Integer
        String[]   asLines asRunLc asNames asSupers asDeclFiles asCand asCandLc asCandFile asCandWhy
        String[][] asObjFiles      // a jagged array is declared one to a line (error 4391 otherwise)
        String[][] asLabelSites
        String[][] asOutside
        String[][] asSites
        Integer[]  aiCount
        String     sClass sClassLc sFn sSuperLc sWhy
        Integer    i j k iLast iCand iTotal iDone
        Boolean    bDeclared

        Move (Trim(sParameter)) to sClass
        Move (Pos(",", sClass)) to i
        If (i > 0) ;
            Move (Trim(Left(sClass, (i - 1)))) to sClass
        Move (Lowercase(sClass)) to sClassLc
        If (ghoFuncLib <> 0) Begin
            Get psExecutionContext of ghoFuncLib to sFn
            If (sFn <> "") ;
                Send SetSummaryUnit of ghoFuncLib sFn "object(s)"
        End

        // PASS 1: the class declarations of the run's files.
        Move (SizeOfArray(asFiles) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(asFiles[i])) to asRunLc[-1]
        Loop
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Mod(i, 20) = 0) ;
                Send _Panel "Looking for grid subclasses in:" asFiles[i] (i + 1) (iLast + 1)
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(asFiles[i])) to asLines
            Send _CollectClassDecls (&asLines) asFiles[i] (&asNames) (&asSupers) (&asDeclFiles)
            If (_CancelAsked(Self) = True) ;
                Function_Return 0
        Loop

        // The classes to convert: the one named, or every grid subclass declared.
        Move False to bDeclared
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asNames) - 1)
            Move (Lowercase(asSupers[i])) to sSuperLc
            If (sClass <> "") Begin
                If (Lowercase(asNames[i]) = sClassLc) Begin
                    Move True to bDeclared
                    Move asNames[i]     to asCand[-1]
                    Move asDeclFiles[i] to asCandFile[-1]
                End
            End
            Else If (sSuperLc = "dbgrid" or sSuperLc = "dblist" or sSuperLc = "grid" or sSuperLc = "list") Begin
                Move asNames[i]     to asCand[-1]
                Move asDeclFiles[i] to asCandFile[-1]
            End
        Loop
        If (sClass <> "" and bDeclared = False) Begin
            Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - Class " + sClass + " is not declared in the selected files. Select the folder of its package as well, and run again.")
            Function_Return 0
        End
        Move (SizeOfArray(asCand)) to iCand
        If (iCand = 0) Begin
            Send _RunNote "No grid subclass is declared in the selected files - nothing to convert."
            Function_Return 0
        End
        For k from 0 to (iCand - 1)
            Move (Lowercase(asCand[k])) to asCandLc[k]
        Loop

        // PASS 2: the files outside the run - classes built on a candidate, objects of one.
        Move (ResizeArray(asOutside, iCand)) to asOutside
        Send _ScanOutsideRun asRunLc (&asCandLc) (&asNames) (&asSupers) (&asDeclFiles) (&asOutside)
        If (_CancelAsked(Self) = True) ;
            Function_Return 0

        // Which of them can be converted at all (SubclassVerdict - the Check asks the same question).
        For k from 0 to (iCand - 1)
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(asCandFile[k])) to asLines
            Get SubclassVerdict (&asLines) asCand[k] (&asNames) (&asSupers) (&asDeclFiles) to sWhy
            Move sWhy to asCandWhy[k]
            // The port's refusal is counted in full in the note; the verdict - what the Check shows - stays its first reason.
            If (sWhy <> "" and sWhy = psRefusal(Self)) ;
                Move (_RefusalSummary(Self)) to sWhy
            If (sWhy <> "") ;
                Send _RunNote ("NOT CONVERTED - " + asCand[k] + " (" + asCandFile[k] + "): " + sWhy + ".")
        Loop

        // PASS 3: the objects of every candidate, one walk per file.
        Move (ResizeArray(asObjFiles, iCand))   to asObjFiles
        Move (ResizeArray(asLabelSites, iCand)) to asLabelSites
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Mod(i, 20) = 0) ;
                Send _Panel "Looking for their objects in:" asFiles[i] (i + 1) (iLast + 1)
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(asFiles[i])) to asLines
            Send _ScanObjectsAll (&asLines) (&asCandLc) (&aiCount) (&asSites)
            For k from 0 to (iCand - 1)
                If (aiCount[k] > 0) Begin
                    Move asFiles[i] to asObjFiles[k][SizeOfArray(asObjFiles[k])]
                    For j from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asSites[k]) - 1)
                        Move (asFiles[i] + " " + asSites[k][j]) to asLabelSites[k][SizeOfArray(asLabelSites[k])]
                    Loop
                End
            Loop
            If (_CancelAsked(Self) = True) ;
                Function_Return 0
        Loop

        // Said once per run, because the run's function list names only this one (Nils 2026-10-05).
        Send _RunNote "This function runs RefactorDbGridTocDbCJGrid, RefactorDbListTocDbCJGridPromptList and RefactorGridToCJGrid itself, on the objects of each class it converts. Their own parameters are not used."

        // Each class in turn. The next one reads what this one wrote.
        Move 0 to iTotal
        For k from 0 to (iCand - 1)
            If (asCandWhy[k] = "") Begin
                Get _ConvertOneClass asCand[k] asCandFile[k] asObjFiles[k] asLabelSites[k] asOutside[k] to iDone
                Add iDone to iTotal
                If (_CancelAsked(Self) = True) ;
                    Function_Return iTotal
            End
        Loop
        If (ghoStatusPanel <> 0) Begin
            Set Title_Text     of ghoStatusPanel to ""
            Set TableName_Text of ghoStatusPanel to ""
        End
        Function_Return iTotal
    End_Function

End_Class
